496
00:39:23,487 --> 00:39:28,158
… commanding officer of the armed forces
of the United States of America.

497
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:32,204
On behalf of the people of Earth,
welcome.

498
00:39:33,330 --> 00:39:34,415
He did that well.

499
00:40:04,987 --> 00:40:07,156
<i>We come in peace.</i>

500
00:40:07,323 --> 00:40:10,659
<i>We come in peace. We come in peace.</i>

501
00:40:14,455 --> 00:40:16,624
They came in peace.

502
00:40:19,793 --> 00:40:21,378
<i>We come in peace.</i>

503
00:40:50,824 --> 00:40:53,243
Open fire!

504
00:41:13,931 --> 00:41:15,224
Whoa!

505
00:41:23,482 --> 00:41:24,608
What the hell is this?

506
00:41:30,489 --> 00:41:31,824
Nathalie!

507
00:42:14,366 --> 00:42:17,202
Die, you alien shithead!

508
00:42:20,748 --> 00:42:22,166
Uh-oh.

509
00:42:23,333 --> 00:42:24,376
I surrender.

510
00:42:32,259 --> 00:42:34,636
No, that ain't happening.
That didn't happen.

511
00:42:48,692 --> 00:42:50,069
Nathalie.

512
00:42:52,613 --> 00:42:53,655
Aah!

513
00:43:31,902 --> 00:43:34,530
Holy mother of God.

514
00:43:34,696 --> 00:43:35,823
Did you see that?

515
00:43:35,989 --> 00:43:38,617
We should hit these assholes
with everything we got, sir.

516
00:43:38,784 --> 00:43:41,411
Sir, Mr. President,
I know this seems terrible…

517
00:43:41,578 --> 00:43:43,622
… but let's not be too rash.

518
00:43:43,789 --> 00:43:45,707
We should nuke them now, sir.

519
00:43:45,874 --> 00:43:48,544
We must establish
a line of communication first.

520
00:43:49,419 --> 00:43:51,004
Why not set up a town hall?

521
00:43:51,171 --> 00:43:53,465
We can get the public's opinion.

522
00:43:55,259 --> 00:43:56,844
What do you think, Marsha?

523
00:43:58,804 --> 00:44:00,305
Kick the crap out of them.

524
00:44:01,765 --> 00:44:03,433
Ladies and gentlemen…

525
00:44:03,600 --> 00:44:05,769
… this could be
a cultural misunderstanding.

526
00:44:06,395 --> 00:44:08,564
Yeah. Maybe to them, doves mean war.

527
00:44:10,941 --> 00:44:14,111
We all saw how they reacted
to that dove.

528
00:44:14,278 --> 00:44:16,029
It frightened them.

529
00:44:16,196 --> 00:44:18,574
He did say that…

530
00:44:20,075 --> 00:44:22,744
… "We come in peace."

531
00:44:23,954 --> 00:44:25,581
Yes.

532
00:44:32,379 --> 00:44:34,464
The new computer's ready,
Mr. President.

533
00:44:34,631 --> 00:44:36,633
Okay, let's do it.

534
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:39,887
I know we're making the right decision.

535
00:44:42,097 --> 00:44:44,433
Ready to transmit.

536
00:44:45,934 --> 00:44:50,063
This is the president
of the United States.

537
00:44:50,772 --> 00:44:52,566
I'm speaking to you in the hope…

538
00:44:52,733 --> 00:44:55,819
… that what happened earlier today
in the Nevada desert…

539
00:44:56,445 --> 00:44:59,948
… was a cultural misunderstanding.

540
00:45:00,115 --> 00:45:02,993
There can be no doubt
that we two peoples…

541
00:45:03,160 --> 00:45:06,455
… have a great deal to offer one another.

542
00:45:06,622 --> 00:45:08,832
You must be as excited as we…

543
00:45:08,999 --> 00:45:12,211
<i>… to find intelligent life
in the solar system.</i>

544
00:45:13,295 --> 00:45:15,297
<i>And let me make it clear:</i>

545
00:45:15,464 --> 00:45:19,426
<i>You have nothing to fear from us.</i>

546
00:45:20,010 --> 00:45:22,721
<i>Our customs may be strange to you…</i>

547
00:45:22,888 --> 00:45:26,808
<i>… but we mean no harm.</i>

548
00:46:37,879 --> 00:46:40,257
When the investors fly in…

549
00:46:40,882 --> 00:46:47,097
… I would like for them each
to be met by a limo.

550
00:46:47,264 --> 00:46:50,183
Top-of-the-line cars…

551
00:46:50,350 --> 00:46:52,894
… leather interiors…

552
00:46:53,061 --> 00:46:55,188
… Corinthian, if they got it.

553
00:46:55,355 --> 00:46:59,818
Art, are you still spinning your wheels
on that cockamamie hotel?

554
00:47:00,152 --> 00:47:02,529
- Whoa.
- Hello.

555
00:47:03,280 --> 00:47:05,407
The Martians have attacked.

556
00:47:05,574 --> 00:47:09,619
This was no misunderstanding.
I was there. I saw it.

557
00:47:09,786 --> 00:47:11,997
Look, you're worried about yesterday.

558
00:47:12,581 --> 00:47:14,583
But I'm worried about tomorrow.

559
00:47:14,750 --> 00:47:18,253
The Martians land on Earth,
they're gonna need a place to stay.

560
00:47:18,420 --> 00:47:19,880
Just like everybody else.

561
00:47:20,797 --> 00:47:22,507
My God.

562
00:47:23,717 --> 00:47:26,720
Maybe we should all be destroyed.

563
00:47:27,554 --> 00:47:30,807
The human race doesn't deserve to live.

564
00:47:37,606 --> 00:47:40,359
Ethel, that reminds me.

565
00:47:40,525 --> 00:47:43,153
I would like for every limo to be stocked…

566
00:47:43,320 --> 00:47:46,615
… with every kind of alcohol
known to man.

567
00:47:46,782 --> 00:47:51,870
And top it off
with a bottle of Dom on ice.

568
00:47:52,120 --> 00:47:55,415
What confounds me most of all,
gentlemen, is the lack of genitalia.

569
00:47:55,582 --> 00:48:00,379
And of course down here we have the aorta.
Up here we have the sphinx.

570
00:48:00,545 --> 00:48:03,715
Notice the highly developed
cranial nerve system here.

571
00:48:03,882 --> 00:48:07,344
This explains, of course,
the cerebral arteries.

572
00:48:07,511 --> 00:48:11,973
And if we notice down here,
behind the optic chiasm…

573
00:48:12,140 --> 00:48:13,725
… several glands…

574
00:48:17,979 --> 00:48:20,482
Very curious.

575
00:49:01,898 --> 00:49:07,446
He who believes in me,
though he die, yet shall he live.

576
00:49:07,612 --> 00:49:11,908
And whoever lives and believes in me
shall never die.

577
00:49:12,993 --> 00:49:16,204
Billy Glenn Norris gave his life
defending our country.

578
00:49:16,371 --> 00:49:17,622
Why did it have to be him?

579
00:49:17,789 --> 00:49:20,250
Billy Glenn Norris is a true American hero.

580
00:49:20,417 --> 00:49:23,003
May God rest his soul.

581
00:49:24,504 --> 00:49:27,048
Ready. Aim.

582
00:49:27,466 --> 00:49:29,134
Fire.

583
00:49:30,051 --> 00:49:32,179
Aim. Fire.

584
00:49:33,722 --> 00:49:36,641
Aim. Fire.

585
00:49:44,900 --> 00:49:46,193
Hello?

586
00:49:46,359 --> 00:49:49,571
Byron. Is everything all right?
You still coming tomorrow?

587
00:49:49,738 --> 00:49:53,283
You just try and stop me.
That plane arrives at 4 p.m.

588
00:49:53,450 --> 00:49:56,578
<i>- Are the kids there?</i>
- Yeah, hold on.

589
00:49:56,745 --> 00:49:58,955
Cedric. Neville.

590
00:50:00,916 --> 00:50:02,792
- Me first.
- No, me.

591
00:50:04,920 --> 00:50:07,422
- Hey, Dad.
- Who's that? Neville?

592
00:50:07,589 --> 00:50:09,466
<i>- Yeah.</i>
- How you doing?

593
00:50:09,633 --> 00:50:13,094
- We're going to the White House.
<i>- You're going to the White House?</i>

594
00:50:13,261 --> 00:50:14,554
Yeah, tomorrow.

595
00:50:14,721 --> 00:50:17,057
- Man, give it back.
- Leave me alone.

596
00:50:17,224 --> 00:50:19,226
It's a school thing, like a tour.

597
00:50:19,392 --> 00:50:22,312
So that means you're still going to school
once in a while?

598
00:50:22,479 --> 00:50:23,647
Yeah.

599
00:50:23,813 --> 00:50:27,484
- Give me your ma again, all right?
- All right. Hold on. Mom.

600
00:50:27,651 --> 00:50:30,820
- You always get to the phone first.
- So what?

601
00:50:30,987 --> 00:50:33,114
Well, I'm first to the game.

602
00:50:34,282 --> 00:50:37,619
What are you wasting this phone time for?
We're gonna see you tomorrow.

603
00:50:37,786 --> 00:50:40,455
Yeah, but there's something
I want to say to you.

604
00:50:40,622 --> 00:50:42,958
Just because I feel like saying it,
all right?

605
00:50:43,124 --> 00:50:44,292
Yeah, what's that?

606
00:50:45,293 --> 00:50:46,503
I love you.

607
00:50:48,463 --> 00:50:50,382
I love you too, Byron.

608
00:50:50,549 --> 00:50:53,468
Now stop wasting money.
I'll see you tomorrow.

609
00:51:11,278 --> 00:51:12,779
They're responding.

610
00:51:15,991 --> 00:51:18,201
A message from the Martians.

611
00:51:20,120 --> 00:51:21,997
- Really?
- They've issued a formal apology.

612
00:51:22,163 --> 00:51:27,377
This is great.

613
00:51:28,003 --> 00:51:29,963
Didn't I tell you this would happen?

614
00:51:30,130 --> 00:51:34,259
The Martian ambassador feels terrible
and asked permission to speak to Congress.

615
00:51:34,426 --> 00:51:36,052
I mean, that's good, isn't it?

616
00:51:36,219 --> 00:51:38,179
You bet.

617
00:51:38,346 --> 00:51:40,682
It's a great victory for our administration.

618
00:52:55,423 --> 00:52:56,549
Ladies and gentlemen.

619
00:52:57,217 --> 00:53:00,095
<i>This is a proud day for all Americans.</i>

620
00:53:00,929 --> 00:53:04,391
This is a hell of a photo op, Jerry.

621
00:53:04,557 --> 00:53:06,768
Are you sure I shouldn't be there?

622
00:53:06,935 --> 00:53:10,730
For some picky reason, the Secret Service
don't want the executive branch…

623
00:53:10,897 --> 00:53:14,818
… and the legislative branch
in the same room at the same time.

624
00:53:14,984 --> 00:53:17,904
The Martian ambassador
is gonna say a few words.

625
00:53:18,446 --> 00:53:20,949
Come on down, Mr. Ambassador.

626
00:54:27,557 --> 00:54:28,683
Oh.

627
00:54:28,850 --> 00:54:31,019
Mr. Ambassador, please!

628
00:54:36,316 --> 00:54:39,444
Mr. Ambassador. What are you doing?
This doesn't make sense!

629
00:54:39,611 --> 00:54:41,696
It's not logical! It's not—

630
00:54:43,823 --> 00:54:45,200
Guess it wasn't the dove.

631
00:54:47,577 --> 00:54:48,995
Fire!

632
00:54:54,125 --> 00:54:55,543
They blew up Congress.

633
00:55:18,107 --> 00:55:20,318
What did they do that for?

634
00:55:20,485 --> 00:55:23,488
Maybe they don't liking
the human being.

635
00:55:41,381 --> 00:55:42,757
Hello, gentlemen.

636
00:55:42,924 --> 00:55:47,095
Nice of you to come
on such short notice.

637
00:55:48,137 --> 00:55:52,100
General Decker,
it seems I owe you an apology.

638
00:55:52,267 --> 00:55:55,019
Hey, we all make mistakes,
Mr. President.

639
00:55:55,186 --> 00:55:57,272
Not anymore.

640
00:55:57,814 --> 00:56:00,650
We're going to take charge of this thing.

641
00:56:00,817 --> 00:56:02,902
Excellent, sir. I have prepared the order.

642
00:56:03,945 --> 00:56:05,113
What's this?

643
00:56:05,280 --> 00:56:09,576
Oh, that's your executive order authorizing
full use of our nuclear deterrent, sir.

644
00:56:12,120 --> 00:56:14,789
Are you out of your mind?
I'm not going to start a war.

645
00:56:14,956 --> 00:56:16,457
We're already at war, sir.

646
00:56:16,624 --> 00:56:18,877
We have to nuke them.
We have to nuke them now!

647
00:56:20,503 --> 00:56:24,007
General Decker, if you do not shut up…

648
00:56:24,173 --> 00:56:26,384
… I'm going to relieve you
of your command.

649
00:56:26,551 --> 00:56:28,386
We have to strike now, sir.

650
00:56:28,553 --> 00:56:30,972
Annihilate. Kill! Kill! Kill!

651
00:56:31,139 --> 00:56:34,767
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

652
00:57:00,335 --> 00:57:01,878
Now…

653
00:57:03,338 --> 00:57:05,465
… I want the people to know…

654
00:57:05,632 --> 00:57:10,011
… that they still have two out of three
branches of government working for them…

655
00:57:10,178 --> 00:57:11,888
… and that ain't bad.

656
00:57:12,180 --> 00:57:17,352
I want the people to know
that the schools will still be open, okay?

657
00:57:17,518 --> 00:57:19,854
And I want the people to know…

658
00:57:20,021 --> 00:57:23,149
… that the garbage
will still be carried out.

659
00:57:23,316 --> 00:57:26,486
And I want a cop on every corner.

660
00:57:26,653 --> 00:57:28,571
Which, incidentally…

661
00:57:28,738 --> 00:57:31,074
… we would already have…

662
00:57:31,240 --> 00:57:34,577
… if they had listened to me
in the last election.

663
00:57:37,330 --> 00:57:38,748
Jerry…

664
00:57:38,915 --> 00:57:41,000
… how soon can we go on the air?

665
00:57:44,003 --> 00:57:45,546
Uh…

666
00:57:46,881 --> 00:57:49,425
My fellow Americans…

667
00:57:49,592 --> 00:57:51,636
… it is with a heavy heart…

668
00:57:51,803 --> 00:57:55,640
<i>… that I speak to you this afternoon.
As you know…</i>

669
00:57:55,807 --> 00:58:00,770
<i>… earlier today the Martian ambassador
and his confederates…</i>

670
00:58:00,937 --> 00:58:07,527
<i>… attacked and killed many
of your representatives on Capitol Hill.</i>

671
00:58:07,694 --> 00:58:11,656
I will be conferring with other world leaders
as time goes on.

672
00:58:11,823 --> 00:58:17,203
And rest assured that,
working together…

673
00:58:17,370 --> 00:58:20,707
… we will soon come out…

674
00:58:20,873 --> 00:58:24,877
… at a very real outcome.

675
00:58:26,254 --> 00:58:27,797
Thank you.

676
00:58:34,971 --> 00:58:36,264
Hmm.

677
00:58:51,279 --> 00:58:52,697
Oh.

678
00:58:54,532 --> 00:58:56,284
Nathalie?

679
00:58:56,743 --> 00:58:58,828
Nathalie, is that you?

680
00:58:58,995 --> 00:59:01,622
Yes. How are you feeling?

681
00:59:03,791 --> 00:59:06,210
Not terribly good, I'm afraid.

682
00:59:07,920 --> 00:59:09,380
May I ask you a question?

683
00:59:09,922 --> 00:59:13,801
Mm. Yes.
Yes, of course you can, Nathalie.

684
00:59:15,094 --> 00:59:17,638
Were you flirting with me on the show?

685
00:59:17,805 --> 00:59:20,475
Because if you were…

686
00:59:20,641 --> 00:59:24,645
… I just want you to know that I liked it.

687
00:59:24,854 --> 00:59:28,066
Ha-ha. You did? Really?

688
00:59:28,232 --> 00:59:31,486
Because, you know,
I've watched you on TV quite a bit…

689
00:59:31,652 --> 00:59:36,783
… and, well, I've had something
of a schoolboy crush on you for…

690
00:59:36,949 --> 00:59:39,994
… oh, gosh, ages.

691
01:00:20,868 --> 01:00:24,372
Hi there.
Are you interested in the White House?

692
01:00:29,627 --> 01:00:31,921
I work there. I'm the press secretary.

693
01:00:32,088 --> 01:00:33,256
My name's Jerry Ross.

694
01:00:34,215 --> 01:00:36,509
Maybe you've heard of me?

695
01:00:37,718 --> 01:00:40,513
You wouldn't believe
the pressure of my job.

696
01:00:42,056 --> 01:00:44,100
It's nice to see a new face.

697
01:00:49,814 --> 01:00:53,276
Hey, are you doing anything?

698
01:00:53,442 --> 01:00:57,488
Because if you want,
I could give you a personalized tour.

699
01:00:57,864 --> 01:00:59,615
Would you like that?

700
01:01:01,784 --> 01:01:05,288
Hey, Mitch, it's me. Can you let me in?

701
01:01:08,708 --> 01:01:10,710
Oh, hello, Mr. Ross. Sure.

702
01:01:10,877 --> 01:01:13,296
We're a little nervous here,
after what happened.

703
01:01:13,462 --> 01:01:15,173
Exactly.

704
01:01:24,098 --> 01:01:27,435
Many great men and women
have passed through here.

705
01:01:27,602 --> 01:01:30,146
Now we're passing through here.

706
01:01:30,313 --> 01:01:32,064
Feels good, don't it?

707
01:01:35,610 --> 01:01:37,904
You're very graceful.

708
01:01:38,404 --> 01:01:39,447
I like that.

709
01:01:47,288 --> 01:01:48,623
<i>Come here.</i>

710
01:02:09,060 --> 01:02:11,312
We call this the Kennedy Room.

711
01:02:15,358 --> 01:02:17,276
Pretty nifty, huh?

712
01:02:50,184 --> 01:02:52,853
So how's about a drink?

713
01:03:22,591 --> 01:03:25,219
Ah. Getting more comfortable, I see.

714
01:03:27,555 --> 01:03:29,515
Outstanding.

715
01:03:43,654 --> 01:03:45,072
How's my lady doing?

716
01:03:55,416 --> 01:03:58,169
Oh, missy, you're hot.

717
01:03:58,336 --> 01:04:00,963
But could we get that gum
out of your mouth?

718
01:04:03,883 --> 01:04:05,343
Oh!

719
01:04:07,345 --> 01:04:08,554
My finger!

720
01:04:13,601 --> 01:04:16,604
Hello? Hello, operator?
Operator, this is an emergency!

721
01:04:16,771 --> 01:04:18,856
Help! Please!

722
01:05:43,983 --> 01:05:45,359
Don't shoot.

723
01:05:49,447 --> 01:05:50,614
Don't worry, darling.

724
01:05:59,540 --> 01:06:00,624
Get down!

725
01:06:11,427 --> 01:06:13,637
- Thank you, Mitch.
- It's my job.

726
01:06:14,138 --> 01:06:16,432
Jimmy. Aah! Jimmy.

727
01:07:08,442 --> 01:07:09,527
What's happening?

728
01:07:09,693 --> 01:07:15,407
They appear to be in a highly agitated state,
Nathalie. And I don't know.

729
01:07:16,075 --> 01:07:17,535
I honestly don't know, Nathalie.

730
01:07:17,701 --> 01:07:20,579
I don't know what's going on anymore.
This is frustrating.

731
01:07:20,746 --> 01:07:24,875
I'm just not feeling myself. Nathalie,
if only I could hold you in my arms.

732
01:07:25,042 --> 01:07:28,504
Oh, Donald. I'm scared.

733
01:08:02,621 --> 01:08:04,707
Excuse me.
But you said you wanted to know…

734
01:08:04,873 --> 01:08:06,959
… as soon as we had an analysis
of the gum.

735
01:08:07,126 --> 01:08:09,295
- What is it?
- It's NO2.

736
01:08:09,461 --> 01:08:11,005
Highly concentrated.

737
01:08:11,171 --> 01:08:13,007
Nitrogen.

738
01:08:13,173 --> 01:08:17,678
So that's how it could breathe
in our atmosphere.

739
01:08:19,013 --> 01:08:20,514
What's that noise?

740
01:08:52,713 --> 01:08:55,549
Theodore, I simply do not feel
that Lincoln…

741
01:08:56,050 --> 01:09:00,054
It's a full-scale invasion. Mr. President,
we're gonna need to get you to safety.

742
01:09:05,559 --> 01:09:06,685
Can we go this way?

743
01:09:06,852 --> 01:09:09,688
Sorry, ma'am.
There's a tour going through here.

744
01:09:09,855 --> 01:09:11,815
The Blue Room is often considered…

745
01:09:11,982 --> 01:09:13,817
… the most beautiful room
in the White House.

746
01:09:13,984 --> 01:09:17,112
In fact, it is often used by the president
to receive guests.

747
01:09:17,279 --> 01:09:19,531
It is furnished to represent the period
of James Monroe.

748
01:09:21,408 --> 01:09:22,743
Hey, what's that?

749
01:09:22,910 --> 01:09:26,789
That is a portrait of James Monroe.

750
01:09:41,512 --> 01:09:42,554
Go, go!

751
01:10:18,799 --> 01:10:20,175
- We lost Taffy.
- Oh, no.

752
01:10:24,638 --> 01:10:28,350
Mr. President, please. Keep moving.
We have to get you to the back stairs!

753
01:10:34,940 --> 01:10:36,442
The Nancy Reagan chandelier.

754
01:10:39,027 --> 01:10:40,487
Marsha!

755
01:10:42,573 --> 01:10:43,574
Marsha!

756
01:10:48,579 --> 01:10:50,372
Marsha?

757
01:10:55,961 --> 01:10:58,839
What are you guys gawking at?
Get that president out of here!

758
01:11:05,220 --> 01:11:07,139
And I personally guarantee…

759
01:11:07,681 --> 01:11:10,058
… that you will get a complete return
on your investment…

760
01:11:11,685 --> 01:11:13,312
… within five months.

761
01:11:13,479 --> 01:11:15,189
Mr. Land, excuse me, please.

762
01:11:15,355 --> 01:11:19,318
Just a second, Sheik Rakmula.

763
01:11:20,736 --> 01:11:26,742
Now, even in a time of so-called
intergalactic emergency…

764
01:11:26,909 --> 01:11:31,997
… the people still wanna roll
them bones.

765
01:11:32,706 --> 01:11:34,416
Mr. Land. I believe—

766
01:11:34,583 --> 01:11:36,502
Just five more minutes, Quinn.

767
01:11:37,336 --> 01:11:39,421
What I would like
for you gentlemen to do…

768
01:11:39,588 --> 01:11:44,968
… is to view our brand-new,
state-of-the-art show room.

769
01:11:45,135 --> 01:11:47,721
It is out of sight.

770
01:11:49,306 --> 01:11:51,225
Gentlemen.

771
01:11:54,311 --> 01:11:57,940
There is no way that we can lose.

772
01:12:01,193 --> 01:12:02,236
Whoa!

773
01:12:43,443 --> 01:12:48,615
<i>It's not unusual to be loved by anyone</i>

774
01:12:48,782 --> 01:12:53,787
<i>It's not unusual to have fun with anyone</i>

775
01:12:53,954 --> 01:12:58,458
<i>But when I see you hanging about
With anyone</i>

776
01:12:59,126 --> 01:13:03,672
<i>It's not unusual to see me cry</i>

777
01:13:03,839 --> 01:13:06,425
<i>I wanna die</i>

778
01:13:06,758 --> 01:13:09,970
I've been trying to call you all day.
The flight's been canceled.

779
01:13:10,137 --> 01:13:12,514
Byron, there's Martians everywhere.

780
01:13:13,891 --> 01:13:15,893
- Hello?
- Byron! Byron!

781
01:13:16,059 --> 01:13:18,854
- I can't hear you!
- Byron!

782
01:13:23,358 --> 01:13:24,735
I gotta get to Washington.

783
01:13:25,402 --> 01:13:27,154
Byron?

784
01:13:28,363 --> 01:13:31,867
Byron? Byron.
Do you know anyone who can fly a plane?

785
01:13:32,034 --> 01:13:34,119
- Yeah, your husband, Art.
- No, he's dead.

786
01:13:34,286 --> 01:13:38,123
I told him this was gonna happen.
I even loaded a plane with supplies.

787
01:13:38,290 --> 01:13:42,711
I want to go to Tahoe, to the Tahoe caves.
It's remote, the Martians won't find it.

788
01:13:42,878 --> 01:13:44,087
Well, where's the plane?

789
01:13:44,254 --> 01:13:47,007
Private airfield.
Other side of the freeway.

790
01:13:47,174 --> 01:13:50,928
- You think they'll fly to Washington, D.C.?
- Why? I wanna go to Tahoe.

791
01:13:51,595 --> 01:13:55,766
<i>You'll find it happens
All the time</i>

792
01:13:55,933 --> 01:14:01,521
<i>Love would never do
What you want it to</i>

793
01:14:01,688 --> 01:14:03,857
<i>Why can't this crazy love</i>

794
01:14:04,441 --> 01:14:08,820
<i>Be mine</i>

795
01:14:15,369 --> 01:14:16,495
Jesus Christ.

796
01:14:25,754 --> 01:14:27,881
Girls, get out! Get out!

797
01:14:30,425 --> 01:14:32,469
Get out! Get out!

798
01:14:36,431 --> 01:14:38,392
There's a Martian right behind me.

799
01:14:38,558 --> 01:14:40,394
Hey, you're Tom Jones, right?

800
01:14:40,727 --> 01:14:42,229
<i>It ain't unusual</i>

801
01:14:42,396 --> 01:14:44,731
Tom, Tom, can I have an autograph?
Anybody got a pen?

802
01:15:04,251 --> 01:15:07,045
- Hey, that was a hell of a punch.
- You'd better get that gun.

803
01:15:07,212 --> 01:15:08,922
- I'm Tom Jones.
- Byron Williams.

804
01:15:09,089 --> 01:15:11,091
Hey, I saw you fight
in Cardiff, Wales once.

805
01:15:11,258 --> 01:15:12,718
- Yeah? Hey, Barbara.
- Yeah?

806
01:15:12,884 --> 01:15:14,136
You all right?

807
01:15:14,302 --> 01:15:16,430
- I need a drink.
- You and me both, baby.

808
01:15:16,596 --> 01:15:18,890
- We better get out.
- You know how to fly a plane?

809
01:15:19,057 --> 01:15:20,809
- Sure. You got one?
- She has.

810
01:15:40,537 --> 01:15:43,081
<i>Don't run, we are your friends.</i>

811
01:16:14,196 --> 01:16:16,573
- Martians blew up the shop.
- You're kidding me?

812
01:16:16,740 --> 01:16:18,617
- Should I get Grandma?
- Forget Grandma.

813
01:16:18,784 --> 01:16:21,453
She's halfway to outer space already.
Here, lock and load.

814
01:16:21,620 --> 01:16:24,790
I'll tell you one thing.
They ain't getting the TV.

815
01:16:28,668 --> 01:16:31,671
<i>The president of France on line two.</i>

816
01:16:35,008 --> 01:16:38,512
<i>Mr. President, the president of France
is on line two.</i>

817
01:16:38,678 --> 01:16:40,680
<i>He says it's important.</i>

818
01:16:46,061 --> 01:16:48,230
Hello, Maurice.

819
01:16:51,316 --> 01:16:54,027
I have some good news for you.
The Martian ambassador is here.

820
01:16:54,194 --> 01:16:57,197
And we've negotiated a settlement.

821
01:16:58,698 --> 01:17:01,701
Maurice, get out of the room.
Get out now.

822
01:17:48,206 --> 01:17:49,291
Mr. President.

823
01:17:51,918 --> 01:17:53,628
Mr. President.

824
01:17:53,795 --> 01:17:56,464
I need you to sign this.

825
01:18:01,261 --> 01:18:02,512
What is it?

826
01:18:02,679 --> 01:18:05,140
My last will and testament?

827
01:18:05,307 --> 01:18:09,269
It is an order to deploy
our nuclear capability, sir.

828
01:18:17,152 --> 01:18:21,823
<i>Three, two, one, fire.</i>

829
01:19:21,341 --> 01:19:23,009
What the hell was that?

830
01:21:05,028 --> 01:21:06,071
Look!

831
01:21:13,953 --> 01:21:15,497
What was that?

832
01:21:17,082 --> 01:21:19,167
- Where you going?
- To go get Grandma.

833
01:21:19,334 --> 01:21:21,336
No, you ain't.
Stay and defend this trailer.

834
01:21:21,503 --> 01:21:23,505
That's what Billy Glenn would've done.

835
01:21:23,671 --> 01:21:27,342
- You leave, you're disgracing a hero.
- I don't care. I'm gonna go get Grandma.

836
01:21:27,509 --> 01:21:30,512
- Boy!
- Richie, come back here!

837
01:21:43,191 --> 01:21:44,567
What in the hell is that?

838
01:21:51,991 --> 01:21:53,952
Hey! Cut it out!

839
01:21:59,499 --> 01:22:00,625
Stop it!

840
01:22:09,634 --> 01:22:11,010
- This way.
- No, this way.

841
01:22:13,304 --> 01:22:16,391
Bullshit! The airfield's over there!

842
01:22:21,146 --> 01:22:24,149
Hey. Hey, just because
you're dressed like King Tut…

843
01:22:24,315 --> 01:22:27,527
… doesn't mean you're our leader.
Look at this. This is wrong!

844
01:22:27,694 --> 01:22:31,114
We're lost. He led us down a maze.
I'm going back to the hotel.

845
01:22:31,281 --> 01:22:33,032
- Come on, this way!
- Wait!

846
01:22:33,199 --> 01:22:36,369
- No, wait! Where are you going?
- Come on, Barbara.

847
01:22:36,536 --> 01:22:38,788
I like him. I do.

848
01:22:44,002 --> 01:22:48,006
Assholes. Why did I listen to them?
I should have stayed in the hotel.

849
01:22:48,548 --> 01:22:50,049
Shit!

850
01:22:52,927 --> 01:22:54,345
I surrender, okay?

851
01:22:54,971 --> 01:22:57,098
You understand what that means?
Surrender?

852
01:22:58,600 --> 01:23:00,977
Lookit. You're intelligent beings.

853
01:23:01,686 --> 01:23:03,855
Let's cut a deal. I can help you.

854
01:23:04,022 --> 01:23:05,773
I'm a lawyer.

855
01:23:05,940 --> 01:23:09,194
You want to conquer the world,
you're gonna need lawyers, right?

856
01:23:10,820 --> 01:23:12,655
Here.

857
01:23:12,822 --> 01:23:14,991
You want my watch?

858
01:23:15,158 --> 01:23:17,494
Take it. Take it. Go on. It's a Rolex.

859
01:23:18,745 --> 01:23:20,872
Rolex.

860
01:23:28,296 --> 01:23:31,090
- Nice shot.
- Yeah, pity I was too late.

861
01:23:31,257 --> 01:23:35,261
Barbara, can I have the gun back, please?
Barbara, give me the gun and come on!

862
01:24:50,044 --> 01:24:51,504
Grandma!

863
01:24:59,178 --> 01:25:00,638
Oh, my God.

864
01:25:10,898 --> 01:25:12,859
<i>When I'm calling you</i>

865
01:25:13,026 --> 01:25:17,113
Richie, I think these guys are very sick.

866
01:25:18,156 --> 01:25:21,409
What's happening to them?
What's killing them?

867
01:25:22,243 --> 01:25:24,537
I think it must be my music.

868
01:25:27,957 --> 01:25:30,418
Ho! Shh! Shh.

869
01:25:32,587 --> 01:25:33,921
Quiet.

870
01:26:25,473 --> 01:26:27,892
You think you can do anything you want.

871
01:26:28,059 --> 01:26:29,435
Well, you can't.

872
01:26:29,602 --> 01:26:34,148
You see, because we are human beings.

873
01:26:34,315 --> 01:26:38,695
And we have the United States Army…

874
01:26:38,861 --> 01:26:44,534
… that'll fight you to the last man.
And we'll never surrender.

875
01:26:48,788 --> 01:26:49,956
Do you hear me?

876
01:26:50,123 --> 01:26:53,000
We'll fight you on the beaches.
We'll fight you on the street.

877
01:26:53,167 --> 01:26:55,670
We will never, never surrender.

878
01:26:55,837 --> 01:27:00,216
Old Glory will win!
Democracy will survive!

879
01:27:00,383 --> 01:27:04,053
We will never, ever surrender!

880
01:27:04,220 --> 01:27:08,599
We will win!
The eagle will be triumphant!

881
01:27:10,476 --> 01:27:11,894
No.

882
01:27:37,670 --> 01:27:41,883
Why are you doing this?

883
01:27:43,342 --> 01:27:44,927
Why?

884
01:27:45,803 --> 01:27:48,973
Isn't the universe big enough…

885
01:27:49,140 --> 01:27:51,267
… for both of us?

886
01:27:54,729 --> 01:27:56,939
What is wrong with you people?

887
01:27:59,817 --> 01:28:01,819
We could work together.

888
01:28:02,695 --> 01:28:04,739
Why be enemies?

889
01:28:05,865 --> 01:28:07,700
Because we're different?

890
01:28:08,701 --> 01:28:10,203
Is that why?

891
01:28:14,540 --> 01:28:17,293
Think of the things that we could do.

892
01:28:18,628 --> 01:28:21,839
Think how strong we would be.

893
01:28:23,341 --> 01:28:25,384
Earth…

894
01:28:25,551 --> 01:28:27,804
… and Mars…

895
01:28:28,721 --> 01:28:29,764
… together.

896
01:28:32,558 --> 01:28:35,895
There is nothing
that we could not accomplish.

897
01:28:36,354 --> 01:28:38,231
Think about it.

898
01:28:40,149 --> 01:28:42,193
Think about it.

899
01:28:43,736 --> 01:28:45,196
Why destroy…

900
01:28:45,905 --> 01:28:48,241
… when you can create?

901
01:28:49,700 --> 01:28:51,994
We can have it all…

902
01:28:52,286 --> 01:28:55,873
… or we can smash it all.

903
01:28:58,292 --> 01:29:02,630
Why can't we work out our differences?

904
01:29:03,506 --> 01:29:08,386
Why can't we work things out?

905
01:29:10,638 --> 01:29:12,974
Little people…

906
01:29:15,101 --> 01:29:20,273
… why can't we all just get along?

907
01:29:46,966 --> 01:29:48,718
What's this?

908
01:30:26,339 --> 01:30:29,008
<i>Don't run. We are your friends.</i>

909
01:30:30,885 --> 01:30:33,262
<i>Don't run. We are your friends.</i>

910
01:30:46,859 --> 01:30:48,986
Next stop, radio station.

911
01:30:51,530 --> 01:30:53,366
There it is.

912
01:30:53,699 --> 01:30:55,117
Let's move it!

913
01:31:13,135 --> 01:31:14,762
Here it is.

914
01:31:15,888 --> 01:31:17,723
Go get it started.
Barbara, go with him.

915
01:31:17,890 --> 01:31:20,059
- Okay.
- Cindy, come with me.

916
01:31:35,449 --> 01:31:38,327
Tom. Are you sure you can fly this?

917
01:31:38,494 --> 01:31:40,579
Yeah, I think so, yeah.

918
01:31:43,124 --> 01:31:44,500
Who put that on?

919
01:31:45,418 --> 01:31:48,504
- It's stuck.
- Cindy, over here.

920
01:31:55,011 --> 01:31:56,804
Shit.

921
01:31:56,971 --> 01:31:59,140
They haven't seen us yet. Come here.

922
01:32:00,057 --> 01:32:02,852
- Cindy. Get in the plane.
- What?

923
01:32:03,019 --> 01:32:04,812
I'm staying. I'll distract them.

924
01:32:04,979 --> 01:32:07,189
The first chance you get, you take off.

925
01:32:07,356 --> 01:32:09,859
- I'm not leaving you.
- Just do it.

926
01:32:10,026 --> 01:32:11,610
I'll draw them away. Now, go.

927
01:32:11,777 --> 01:32:14,447
- No.
- I said, go!

928
01:32:19,452 --> 01:32:21,037
Oh, my God.

929
01:32:21,954 --> 01:32:24,081
- What's he doing?
- He must have flipped!

930
01:32:24,248 --> 01:32:27,293
- He's going to throw them off.
- Yeah, but we can't leave him.

931
01:32:30,880 --> 01:32:34,300
No weapon. No clown outfit.

932
01:32:34,467 --> 01:32:36,302
Just me!

933
01:32:36,469 --> 01:32:38,471
Byron Williams…

934
01:32:38,637 --> 01:32:40,681
… heavyweight champion…

935
01:32:41,474 --> 01:32:43,142
… of the world.

936
01:33:53,921 --> 01:33:55,965
Something's happened.

937
01:33:56,132 --> 01:33:58,217
Something's happened to Byron.

938
01:34:15,025 --> 01:34:17,862
<i>When I'm calling you</i>

939
01:34:27,955 --> 01:34:30,082
<i>Will you answer too</i>

940
01:34:39,091 --> 01:34:43,929
<i>That means I offer my love</i>

941
01:35:02,781 --> 01:35:06,076
<i>Our love will come true</i>

942
01:35:08,996 --> 01:35:12,082
<i>You belong to me</i>

943
01:35:12,249 --> 01:35:18,631
<i>I belong to you</i>

944
01:35:20,633 --> 01:35:23,886
Goodbye, my darling.
I wish things could've been different.

945
01:35:24,053 --> 01:35:25,596
So do I.

946
01:35:31,310 --> 01:35:32,811
Goodbye.

947
01:35:32,978 --> 01:35:36,440
- I love you.
- I love you too, Nathalie.

948
01:37:11,952 --> 01:37:13,370
Florence Norris…

949
01:37:13,537 --> 01:37:16,540
… I hereby present to you
the Congressional Medal of Honor…

950
01:37:16,707 --> 01:37:19,084
… the highest decoration
our nation can bestow.

951
01:37:21,086 --> 01:37:24,548
Thank you, honey.
But don't you dare let this happen again.

952
01:37:26,133 --> 01:37:27,843
Richard Norris…

953
01:37:28,010 --> 01:37:31,221
… on behalf of my parents,
who couldn't be here today…

954
01:37:31,388 --> 01:37:33,599
… for saving the world
from the Martians…

955
01:37:33,766 --> 01:37:36,602
… I proudly present to you
the Medal of Honor.

956
01:37:36,769 --> 01:37:38,937
You don't have to kiss me
if you don't want to.

957
01:37:39,730 --> 01:37:41,523
I have to.

958
01:37:44,234 --> 01:37:46,487
I prepared a speech. Is that all right?

959
01:37:47,571 --> 01:37:49,323
Sure, that's very appropriate.

960
01:37:54,203 --> 01:37:56,080
Hi, everybody.

961
01:37:56,914 --> 01:37:58,290
First, I just want to say—

962
01:37:58,457 --> 01:38:01,293
Can you speak up? We can't hear you.

963
01:38:01,460 --> 01:38:04,630
Well, I want to say that there's
a lot of people in the world…

964
01:38:04,797 --> 01:38:07,257
… that have, like,
done a lot more than I have…

965
01:38:07,424 --> 01:38:12,304
… and they're the ones
that should be here now getting a medal.

966
01:38:13,639 --> 01:38:18,227
And I want to thank my grandma
for always being so good to me…

967
01:38:18,394 --> 01:38:22,272
… and for helping save the world
and everything.

968
01:38:22,439 --> 01:38:25,818
So I guess, like, now we just have to…

969
01:38:25,984 --> 01:38:29,988
… start over and start rebuilding everything,
like our houses.

970
01:38:30,155 --> 01:38:33,909
But I was thinking, maybe instead
of houses, we could live in tepees…

971
01:38:34,076 --> 01:38:37,830
… because it's better in a lot of ways.

972
01:38:41,291 --> 01:38:44,294
Okay, that's all I have to say. Thanks.

973
01:38:46,004 --> 01:38:48,882
- Was that okay?
- Yeah.

974
01:38:49,049 --> 01:38:50,801
Do you got a girlfriend?

975
01:38:50,968 --> 01:38:52,553
No.

976
01:38:53,303 --> 01:38:56,807
Guys, come on. Give me a break.
Go on in there and start cleaning your room.

977
01:38:56,974 --> 01:39:00,018
I can't do all this by myself.
Please? Look at you.

978
01:40:17,679 --> 01:40:18,722
Yeah.

